// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-06 | Modified: 2022-06-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects the use of the filename DumpStack.log to evade Microsoft Defender
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/mrd0x/status/1479094189048713219
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_dumpstack_log_evasion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\DumpStack.log" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -o DumpStack.log"
